Answer: To compute the product $374 \times 328$, we break each number into factors:
$$\begin{align*}
374 &= 2 \times 187 \qquad \text{factor 1} \\
328 &= 4 \times 82 \qquad \text{factor 2} \\
\end{align*}$$
The product is the product of the factors: 
$$\begin{align*}
374 \times 328 &= (2 \times 187) \times (4 \times 82)
\end{align*}$$
Apply the associative and commutative properties to help expand this into simpler factors
$$\begin{align*}
(2 \times 187) \times (4 \times 82) &= (187 \times 4) \times (82 \times 2) \\
&= \boxed{(748 \times 84)}
\end{align*}$$
$\bm{(748 \times 84)}$  or $\bm{63312}$.
$$\begin{align*}
374 \times 328 &= (748 \times 84) \\
&= \boxed{63312}
\end{align*}$$
The number is $63312$.
